{"type":"new","contents":"import InfoGeometry.Canonical.BogoliubovVielbein\nimport InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelationalInformationCore\nimport InfoGeometry.Canonical.InformationPartitionCore\n\nopen scoped InnerProductSpace\n\n/-!\n# InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelationalInformationDynamics\n\nConstructive transport layer for operatorial relational information geometry on\nthe doubled carrier.\n\nThis file does not introduce a new scalar facade. It works directly with:\n\n- normalized operator-valued Massieu/log-partition potentials,\n- exact exponential transport of doubled-space endomorphisms,\n- commutator-defined first and second information variations,\n- the QGT metric/phase readouts of those variations,\n- and a concrete realization of the abstract relational-information datum.\n-/\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelationalInformationDynamics\n\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelationalInformationCore\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.StateDependentTransport\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.BogoliubovTransport\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.BogoliubovVielbein.BogoliubovVielbeinBundle\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.InformationCalculus.ModularRadonNikodymData\nopen InfoGeometry.Quantum.GeometricQuantumTensor\nopen InfoGeometry.Krein\n\nsection Core\n\nvariable {E : Type 0}\nvariable [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [CompleteSpace E]\n\nlocal notation \"H₂\" => DoubledSpace E\nlocal notation \"EndH\" => H₂ →L[ℝ] H₂\n\nnoncomputable local instance : NormedRing EndH := inferInstance\nnoncomputable local instance : NormedAlgebra ℝ EndH := inferInstance\nnoncomputable local instance : NormedSpace ℝ EndH := inferInstance\nlocal instance : IsTopologicalRing EndH := inferInstance\nlocal instance : CompleteSpace EndH := inferInstance\n\n/--\nOperatorial exponential chart generated by `K`.\n\nThis is the Lie-theoretic exponential side of the Massieu/log-generating\npicture: a generator `K` is sent to the exponential orbit `τ ↦ exp(τK)`.\nThe inverse logarithmic coordinate is represented in this file by carrying the\ngenerator `K` itself and reading it through the log-partition functional below;\nno global `log (exp K) = K` theorem is asserted without spectral/domain data.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def operatorExponentialChart\n    (K : EndH) : ℝ → EndH :=\n  fun τ => NormedSpace.exp (τ • K)\n\nomit [CompleteSpace E] in\n@[rep_depth operator, simp]\ntheorem operatorExponentialChart_zero\n    (K : EndH) :\n    operatorExponentialChart (E := E) K 0 = 1 := by\n  simp [operatorExponentialChart]\n\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem hasDerivAt_operatorExponentialChart_zero\n    (K : EndH) :\n    HasDerivAt (operatorExponentialChart (E := E) K) K 0 := by\n  simpa [operatorExponentialChart] using\n    (hasDerivAt_exp_smul_const (x := K) (t := (0 : ℝ)))\n\n/-- Analytic log-partition potential attached to an operatorial observable seed. -/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def operatorMassieuPotential\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (A : EndH) : ℝ → ℝ :=\n  fun τ => logInformationPartitionFunction (E := E) ω A τ\n\n/--\nOperatorial log-generating potential.\n\nThis is the Massieu/log-partition functional evaluated on the exponential chart\nof a generator:\n\n`Φ_K(τ) = log ω(exp(τK))`.\n\nIt is the source-faithful formalization of the statement that the\nlog-generating potential is the logarithmic readout dual to the Lie\nexponential map.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def operatorLogGeneratingPotential\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (K : EndH) : ℝ → ℝ :=\n  fun τ => Real.log (ω (operatorExponentialChart (E := E) K τ))\n\n@[rep_depth operator, simp]\ntheorem operatorLogGeneratingPotential_eq_operatorMassieuPotential\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (K : EndH) :\n    operatorLogGeneratingPotential (E := E) ω K\n      =\n    operatorMassieuPotential (E := E) ω K := by\n  funext τ\n  rfl\n\n@[rep_depth operator, simp]\ntheorem informationPartitionFunction_eq_exponentialChart_readout\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (K : EndH) (τ : ℝ) :\n    informationPartitionFunction (E := E) ω K τ\n      =\n    ω (operatorExponentialChart (E := E) K τ) := by\n  rfl\n\n/--\nPrimitive operatorial Massieu value.\n\nThis file treats the normalized infinitesimal observable value `ω(A)` as the\nprimitive functional quantity. Any analytic derivative statement about the\nlog-partition potential is only a witness for this algebraic value.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\nnoncomputable def operatorMassieuExpectation\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (A : EndH) : ℝ :=\n  ω A\n\n/--\nNormalized analytic witness for the primitive operatorial Massieu value.\n\nUnder normalization, the log-partition potential has infinitesimal value\nexactly equal to the observable expectation `ω(A)`.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem operatorMassieuPotential_normalizedInfinitesimalLaw\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (A : EndH)\n    (hω1 : ω (1 : EndH) = 1) :\n    HasDerivAt (operatorMassieuPotential (E := E) ω A)\n      (operatorMassieuExpectation ω A) 0 := by\n  simpa [operatorMassieuPotential, operatorMassieuExpectation] using\n    (hasDerivAt_logInformationPartitionFunction_zero_of_normalized\n      (E := E) (ω := ω) (K := A) hω1)\n\n/--\nInfinitesimal law for the operatorial log-generating potential.\n\nAt the identity of the exponential chart, the derivative of\n`τ ↦ log ω(exp(τK))` is the primitive operatorial Massieu expectation `ω K`\nunder normalized readout `ω(1)=1`.\n-/\n@[rep_depth operator]\ntheorem operatorLogGeneratingPotential_normalizedInfinitesimalLaw\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (K : EndH)\n    (hω1 : ω (1 : EndH) = 1) :\n    HasDerivAt (operatorLogGeneratingPotential (E := E) ω K)\n      (operatorMassieuExpectation ω K) 0 := by\n  rw [operatorLogGeneratingPotential_eq_operatorMassieuPotential]\n  exact operatorMassieuPotential_normalizedInfinitesimalLaw\n    (E := E) ω K hω1\n\n/-- First information variation of an observable seed along a transport channel. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable abbrev operatorInformationFirstVariation\n    (X A : EndH) : EndH :=\n  transportCommutator (E := E) X A\n\n/-- Lie derivation of observables generated by the transport channel `X`. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable def observableLieDerivation\n    (X : EndH) : EndH →ₗ[ℝ] EndH :=\n  InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelationalInformationCore.perturbationDerivation\n    (E := E) X\n\n@[rep_depth transport, simp] theorem observableLieDerivation_apply\n    (X A : EndH) :\n    observableLieDerivation (E := E) X A\n      =\n    operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A := by\n  simp [observableLieDerivation, operatorInformationFirstVariation,\n    InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelationalInformationCore.perturbationDerivation,\n    lieBracket_eq_transportCommutator]\n\n/--\nThe first information variation as a linear map in the perturbation channel for\na fixed observable seed.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable def operatorInformationFirstVariationMap\n    (A : EndH) : PerturbationChannel E →ₗ[ℝ] EndH :=\n  { toFun := fun X => operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A\n    map_add' := by\n      intro X Y\n      apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext\n      intro u\n      apply DoubledSpace.ext <;>\n        simp [operatorInformationFirstVariation, transportCommutator,\n          sub_eq_add_neg, ContinuousLinearMap.add_comp,\n          ContinuousLinearMap.comp_add]\n      · abel\n      · abel\n    map_smul' := by\n      intro c X\n      apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext\n      intro u\n      apply DoubledSpace.ext <;>\n        simp [operatorInformationFirstVariation, transportCommutator,\n          ContinuousLinearMap.smul_comp, smul_sub] }\n\n@[rep_depth transport] theorem operatorInformationFirstVariationMap_apply\n    (A X : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationFirstVariationMap (E := E) A X\n      =\n    operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A := rfl\n\n/-- Mixed second information variation along two transport channels. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable abbrev operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation\n    (X Y A : EndH) : EndH :=\n  transportCommutator (E := E) X (operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) Y A)\n\n/--\nThe mixed second information variation as a canonical bilinear map on\nperturbation channels for a fixed observable seed.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable def operatorInformationMixedSecondVariationMap\n    (A : EndH) :\n    PerturbationChannel E →ₗ[ℝ] PerturbationChannel E →ₗ[ℝ] EndH :=\n  LinearMap.mk₂ ℝ\n    (fun X Y => operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation (E := E) X Y A)\n    (by\n      intro X1 X2 Y\n      apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext\n      intro u\n      apply DoubledSpace.ext <;>\n        simp [operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation, operatorInformationFirstVariation,\n          transportCommutator, sub_eq_add_neg, ContinuousLinearMap.add_comp,\n          ContinuousLinearMap.comp_add]\n      · abel\n      · abel)\n    (by\n      intro c X Y\n      apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext\n      intro u\n      apply DoubledSpace.ext <;>\n        simp [operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation, operatorInformationFirstVariation,\n          transportCommutator, ContinuousLinearMap.smul_comp, smul_sub])\n    (by\n      intro X Y1 Y2\n      apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext\n      intro u\n      apply DoubledSpace.ext <;>\n        simp [operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation, operatorInformationFirstVariation,\n          transportCommutator, sub_eq_add_neg, ContinuousLinearMap.add_comp,\n          ContinuousLinearMap.comp_add]\n      · abel\n      · abel)\n    (by\n      intro c X Y\n      apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext\n      intro u\n      apply DoubledSpace.ext <;>\n        simp [operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation, operatorInformationFirstVariation,\n          transportCommutator, ContinuousLinearMap.smul_comp, smul_sub])\n\n@[rep_depth transport] theorem operatorInformationMixedSecondVariationMap_apply\n    (A X Y : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationMixedSecondVariationMap (E := E) A X Y\n      =\n    operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation (E := E) X Y A := rfl\n\n/-- Nested Lie derivation channel generated by `X` after `Y`. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable def observableLieHessian\n    (X Y : EndH) : EndH →ₗ[ℝ] EndH :=\n  (observableLieDerivation (E := E) X).comp\n    (observableLieDerivation (E := E) Y)\n\n@[rep_depth transport, simp] theorem observableLieHessian_apply\n    (X Y A : EndH) :\n    observableLieHessian (E := E) X Y A\n      =\n    operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation (E := E) X Y A := by\n  simp [observableLieHessian, LinearMap.comp_apply,\n    operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation]\n\n/-- Diagonal second information variation of an observable seed. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable abbrev operatorInformationHessian\n    (X A : EndH) : EndH :=\n  operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation (E := E) X X A\n\nomit [CompleteSpace E] in\n/--\nOwner-form double Lie derivation identity.\n\nThe diagonal information Hessian is exactly the nested transport commutator\n`ad_X²(A) = [X,[X,A]]` in the repo's transport convention. This is the\noperator-valued layer; scalar log-readout norms must be bridged to this theorem\nrather than replacing it.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem operatorInformationHessian_eq_double_transportCommutator\n    (X A : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationHessian (E := E) X A\n      =\n    transportCommutator (E := E) X\n      (transportCommutator (E := E) X A) := by\n  rfl\n\n/--\nSame identity through the named Lie-derivation linear map.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem operatorInformationHessian_eq_observableLieHessian\n    (X A : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationHessian (E := E) X A\n      =\n    observableLieHessian (E := E) X X A := by\n  rw [observableLieHessian_apply]\n\n/-- Symmetric operator-valued second-variation sector. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable def operatorInformationMetricPart\n    (X Y A : EndH) : EndH :=\n  ((2 : ℝ)⁻¹) •\n    (operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation (E := E) X Y A\n      + operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation (E := E) Y X A)\n\n/--\nThe symmetric operator-valued second-variation sector as a canonical bilinear\nmap on perturbation channels.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable def operatorInformationMetricPartMap\n    (A : EndH) :\n    PerturbationChannel E →ₗ[ℝ] PerturbationChannel E →ₗ[ℝ] EndH :=\n  ((2 : ℝ)⁻¹) •\n    (operatorInformationMixedSecondVariationMap (E := E) A\n      + (operatorInformationMixedSecondVariationMap (E := E) A).flip)\n\n@[rep_depth transport] theorem operatorInformationMetricPartMap_apply\n    (A X Y : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationMetricPartMap (E := E) A X Y\n      =\n    operatorInformationMetricPart (E := E) X Y A := by\n  simp [operatorInformationMetricPartMap, operatorInformationMetricPart,\n    operatorInformationMixedSecondVariationMap_apply]\n\n/-- Antisymmetric operator-valued second-variation sector. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable def operatorInformationCurvaturePart\n    (X Y A : EndH) : EndH :=\n  operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation (E := E) X Y A\n    - operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation (E := E) Y X A\n\n/--\nThe antisymmetric operator-valued second-variation sector as a canonical\nbilinear map on perturbation channels.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable def operatorInformationCurvaturePartMap\n    (A : EndH) :\n    PerturbationChannel E →ₗ[ℝ] PerturbationChannel E →ₗ[ℝ] EndH :=\n  operatorInformationMixedSecondVariationMap (E := E) A\n    - (operatorInformationMixedSecondVariationMap (E := E) A).flip\n\n@[rep_depth transport] theorem operatorInformationCurvaturePartMap_apply\n    (A X Y : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationCurvaturePartMap (E := E) A X Y\n      =\n    operatorInformationCurvaturePart (E := E) X Y A := by\n  simp [operatorInformationCurvaturePartMap, operatorInformationCurvaturePart,\n    operatorInformationMixedSecondVariationMap_apply]\n\n@[rep_depth transport] theorem operatorInformationMetricPartMap_diag\n    (A X : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationMetricPartMap (E := E) A X X\n      =\n    operatorInformationHessian (E := E) X A := by\n  simpa [operatorInformationMetricPartMap_apply, operatorInformationMetricPart,\n    operatorInformationHessian, invOf_eq_inv] using\n    invOf_two_smul_add_invOf_two_smul ℝ\n      (operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation (E := E) X X A)\n\n@[rep_depth transport] theorem operatorInformationCurvaturePartMap_diag\n    (A X : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationCurvaturePartMap (E := E) A X X = 0 := by\n  simp [operatorInformationCurvaturePartMap_apply, operatorInformationCurvaturePart]\n\n/-!\nThe curvature channel is algebraic: it is the bracket derivation mandated by\nJacobi, not a background spacetime curvature tensor.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem operatorInformationCurvaturePart_eq_bracketDerivation\n    (X Y A : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationCurvaturePart (E := E) X Y A\n      =\n    observableLieDerivation (E := E) ⁅X, Y⁆ A := by\n  have hFlat :\n      operatorInformationCurvaturePart (E := E) X Y A\n        - observableLieDerivation (E := E) ⁅X, Y⁆ A = 0 := by\n    simpa [operatorInformationCurvaturePart, operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation,\n      observableLieDerivation, operatorInformationFirstVariation,\n      InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelationalInformationCore.transportObstruction,\n      InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelationalInformationCore.perturbationDerivation,\n      lieBracket_eq_transportCommutator] using\n      (InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelationalInformationCore.transportObstruction_eq_zero\n        (E := E) X Y A)\n  exact sub_eq_zero.mp hFlat\n\n/-- Exponential transport path of an observable seed along a transport channel. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable def transportedObservable\n    (X A : EndH) (t : ℝ) : EndH :=\n  InfoGeometry.Canonical.expTransport (A := EndH) X A t\n\n/-- Primitive operatorial Massieu value along the exponential transport orbit. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable def transportedMassieuExpectation\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (X A : EndH) (t : ℝ) : ℝ :=\n  ω (transportedObservable (E := E) X A t)\n\n/--\nScalar logarithmic readout of the transported observable.\n\nThis is only the scalar readout layer over the already-defined operator\ntransport. Its derivative facts below are proved from the exponential\nconjugation commutator law; no coordinate derivative or ambient operator norm is\nintroduced here.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable def scalarLogTransportReadout\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (X A : EndH) (t : ℝ) : ℝ :=\n  Real.log (transportedMassieuExpectation (E := E) ω X A t)\n\n/--\nThe scalar readout of the exponential transport has first derivative equal to\nthe readout of the Lie-derivation first variation.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem hasDerivAt_transportedMassieuExpectation_zero\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (X A : EndH) :\n    HasDerivAt\n      (fun t : ℝ => transportedMassieuExpectation (E := E) ω X A t)\n      (ω (operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A))\n      0 := by\n  have hω : HasDerivAt (fun _ : ℝ => ω) (0 : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) 0 := by\n    simpa using (hasDerivAt_const (x := (0 : ℝ)) (c := ω))\n  have hExp :\n      HasDerivAt\n        (fun t : ℝ => transportedObservable (E := E) X A t)\n        ⁅X, A⁆\n        0 := by\n    simpa [transportedObservable] using\n      (InfoGeometry.Canonical.hasDerivAt_expTransport_at_zero\n        (A := EndH) X A)\n  have hApply :\n      HasDerivAt\n        (fun t : ℝ =>\n          (fun _ : ℝ => ω) t (transportedObservable (E := E) X A t))\n        ((0 : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (transportedObservable (E := E) X A 0)\n          + ω ⁅X, A⁆)\n        0 :=\n    hω.clm_apply hExp\n  have hLie : ⁅X, A⁆ = operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A := by\n    exact lieBracket_eq_transportCommutator (E := E) X A\n  simpa [transportedMassieuExpectation, hLie] using hApply\n\n/--\nThe scalar logarithmic transport readout differentiates to the normalized\nfirst Lie-variation readout. The denominator is the actual readout `ω A`; no\nplaceholder zero or metric shim is inserted.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem hasDerivAt_scalarLogTransportReadout_zero\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (X A : EndH)\n    (hωA : ω A ≠ 0) :\n    HasDerivAt\n      (fun t : ℝ => scalarLogTransportReadout (E := E) ω X A t)\n      ((ω A)⁻¹ * ω (operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A))\n      0 := by\n  have hReadout :\n      HasDerivAt\n        (fun t : ℝ => transportedMassieuExpectation (E := E) ω X A t)\n        (ω (operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A))\n        0 :=\n    hasDerivAt_transportedMassieuExpectation_zero (E := E) ω X A\n  have hLog :\n      HasDerivAt Real.log\n        ((transportedMassieuExpectation (E := E) ω X A 0)⁻¹)\n        (transportedMassieuExpectation (E := E) ω X A 0) := by\n    exact Real.hasDerivAt_log (by\n      simpa [transportedMassieuExpectation, transportedObservable,\n        InfoGeometry.Canonical.expTransport] using hωA)\n  have hComp :\n      HasDerivAt\n        (fun t : ℝ =>\n          Real.log (transportedMassieuExpectation (E := E) ω X A t))\n        ((transportedMassieuExpectation (E := E) ω X A 0)⁻¹\n          * ω (operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A))\n        0 :=\n    hLog.comp 0 hReadout\n  simpa [scalarLogTransportReadout, transportedMassieuExpectation,\n    transportedObservable, InfoGeometry.Canonical.expTransport] using hComp\n\n/--\nThe Lie derivation generated by `X` intertwines with the exponential transport\ngenerated by the same `X`.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem observableLieDerivation_transport_intertwines\n    (X A : EndH) (t : ℝ) :\n    operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X\n      (transportedObservable (E := E) X A t)\n      =\n    transportedObservable (E := E) X\n      (operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A) t := by\n  simpa [operatorInformationFirstVariation, transportedObservable] using\n    (transportCommutator_expTransport (E := E) X A t)\n\n/--\nThe diagonal nested Lie derivation is transported exactly by the same\nexponential orbit.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem observableLieHessian_transport_intertwines\n    (X A : EndH) (t : ℝ) :\n    operatorInformationHessian (E := E) X\n      (transportedObservable (E := E) X A t)\n      =\n    transportedObservable (E := E) X\n      (operatorInformationHessian (E := E) X A) t := by\n  unfold operatorInformationHessian operatorInformationMixedSecondVariation\n  rw [observableLieDerivation_transport_intertwines (E := E)\n    (X := X) (A := A) (t := t)]\n  exact observableLieDerivation_transport_intertwines (E := E)\n    (X := X) (A := operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A) (t := t)\n\n/--\nObservable expectations respect the derivation/transport intertwining law.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem operatorMassieuExpectation_transport_intertwines_firstVariation\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (X A : EndH) (t : ℝ) :\n    transportedMassieuExpectation (E := E) ω X\n      (operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A) t\n      =\n    ω\n      (operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X\n        (transportedObservable (E := E) X A t)) := by\n  simpa [transportedMassieuExpectation] using\n    congrArg ω\n      (observableLieDerivation_transport_intertwines (E := E)\n        (X := X) (A := A) (t := t)).symm\n\n/--\nObservable expectations also respect the transported diagonal Hessian channel.\n-/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem operatorMassieuExpectation_transport_intertwines_hessian\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) (X A : EndH) (t : ℝ) :\n    transportedMassieuExpectation (E := E) ω X\n      (operatorInformationHessian (E := E) X A) t\n      =\n    ω\n      (operatorInformationHessian (E := E) X\n        (transportedObservable (E := E) X A t)) := by\n  simpa [transportedMassieuExpectation] using\n    congrArg ω\n      (observableLieHessian_transport_intertwines (E := E)\n        (X := X) (A := A) (t := t)).symm\n\n/-- Metric readout of the first operatorial information variation. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable def operatorInformationMetricReadout\n    (X A : EndH) : LinearMap.BilinForm ℝ H₂ :=\n  InfoGeometry.Quantum.GeometricQuantumTensor.metricOfOperator\n    (E := E) (operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A)\n\n/-- `(Jε)`-phase readout of the first operatorial information variation. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\nnoncomputable def operatorInformationPhaseReadout\n    (X A : EndH) : LinearMap.BilinForm ℝ H₂ :=\n  InfoGeometry.Quantum.GeometricQuantumTensor.berryOfOperator\n    (E := E) (operatorInformationFirstVariation (E := E) X A)\n\n/-- Channel bilinear form induced by evaluating perturbation channels on a fixed doubled state. -/\n@[rep_depth krein]\nnoncomputable def channelMetricAtState\n    (ψ : H₂) : LinearMap.BilinForm ℝ (PerturbationChannel E) :=\n  LinearMap.mk₂ ℝ\n    (fun X Y => ⟪X ψ, Y ψ⟫_ℝ)\n    (by\n      intro X₁ X₂ Y\n      simp [inner_add_left])\n    (by\n      intro c X Y\n      simp [real_inner_smul_left]\n      ring)\n    (by\n      intro X Y₁ Y₂\n      simp [inner_add_right])\n    (by\n      intro c X Y\n      simp [real_inner_smul_right]\n      ring)\n\n@[rep_depth krein, simp] theorem channelMetricAtState_apply\n    (ψ : H₂) (X Y : PerturbationChannel E) :\n    channelMetricAtState (E := E) ψ X Y = ⟪X ψ, Y ψ⟫_ℝ := rfl\n\n/-- Evaluation at a fixed doubled state as a linear map on perturbation channels. -/\n@[rep_depth krein]\nnoncomputable def channelEvalAtState\n    (ψ : H₂) : PerturbationChannel E →ₗ[ℝ] H₂ :=\n  (ContinuousLinearMap.coeLM (R := ℝ) (S := ℝ) (M := H₂) (N₃ := H₂)).flip ψ\n\n@[rep_depth krein, simp] theorem channelEvalAtState_apply\n    (ψ : H₂) (X : PerturbationChannel E) :\n    channelEvalAtState (E := E) ψ X = X ψ := rfl\n\n/--\nKrein/Hessian channel bilinear form induced by evaluating perturbation channels\non a fixed doubled state.\n\nThis is the relational counterpart of the Noether `fisherBilinAt` surface. It\nis intentionally separate from `channelMetricAtState`, which uses the positive\nHilbert inner product.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein]\nnoncomputable def channelKreinMetricAtState\n    (ψ : H₂) : LinearMap.BilinForm ℝ (PerturbationChannel E) :=\n  (KreinSpace.kreinBilin (H := H₂)).comp\n    (channelEvalAtState (E := E) ψ)\n    (channelEvalAtState (E := E) ψ)\n\n@[rep_depth krein, simp] theorem channelKreinMetricAtState_apply\n    (ψ : H₂) (X Y : PerturbationChannel E) :\n    channelKreinMetricAtState (E := E) ψ X Y\n      =\n    hessian_indefinite_form (E := E) (X ψ) (Y ψ) := by\n  simp [channelKreinMetricAtState, hessian_indefinite_form,\n    LinearMap.BilinForm.comp_apply, channelEvalAtState, KreinSpace.kreinBilin]\n\n/-- Concrete constructive realization of the abstract relational-information datum. -/\n@[rep_depth krein]\nnoncomputable def constructiveRelationalDatum\n    (reference comparison : H₂)\n    (M : StateModularDatum E)\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) :\n    RelationalInformationDatum (E := E) where\n  referenceState := reference\n  comparisonState := comparison\n  modularData := M\n  informationFunctional := fun ψ =>\n    operatorMassieuExpectation ω (stateRelativeModularGenerator (E := E) M ψ)\n  firstVariation := fun ψ A =>\n    ω (stateInducedDynamics (E := E) M ψ A)\n  secondVariation := fun ψ =>\n    channelMetricAtState (E := E) ψ\n\n/--\nThe realized information functional is the primitive operatorial Massieu\nexpectation of the state-relative modular generator.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein, simp]\ntheorem constructiveRelationalDatum_informationFunctional\n    (reference comparison : H₂)\n    (M : StateModularDatum E)\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ)\n    (ψ : H₂) :\n    (constructiveRelationalDatum (E := E) reference comparison M ω).informationFunctional ψ\n      =\n    ω (stateRelativeModularGenerator (E := E) M ψ) := by\n  rfl\n\n/--\nReference functional value of the realized datum is the primitive expectation\nof the reference-state modular generator.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein, simp]\ntheorem constructiveRelationalDatum_referenceFunctionalValue\n    (reference comparison : H₂)\n    (M : StateModularDatum E)\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) :\n    referenceFunctionalValue\n        (constructiveRelationalDatum (E := E) reference comparison M ω)\n      =\n    ω (stateRelativeModularGenerator (E := E) M reference) := by\n  rfl\n\n/--\nComparison functional value of the realized datum is the primitive expectation\nof the comparison-state modular generator.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein, simp]\ntheorem constructiveRelationalDatum_comparisonFunctionalValue\n    (reference comparison : H₂)\n    (M : StateModularDatum E)\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ) :\n    comparisonFunctionalValue\n        (constructiveRelationalDatum (E := E) reference comparison M ω)\n      =\n    ω (stateRelativeModularGenerator (E := E) M comparison) := by\n  rfl\n\n/-- Comparison-state channel metric of the realized datum is the state-evaluated channel bilinear form. -/\n@[rep_depth krein, simp]\ntheorem constructiveRelationalDatum_comparisonGeneratorMetric_apply\n    (reference comparison : H₂)\n    (M : StateModularDatum E)\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ)\n    (X Y : PerturbationChannel E) :\n    comparisonGeneratorMetric\n        (constructiveRelationalDatum (E := E) reference comparison M ω) X Y\n      =\n    ⟪X comparison, Y comparison⟫_ℝ := by\n  simp [comparisonGeneratorMetric, constructiveRelationalDatum, channelMetricAtState]\n\n/-- The comparison-state first variation of the realized datum is the expected induced dynamics. -/\n@[rep_depth transport, simp]\ntheorem constructiveRelationalDatum_firstVariation_comparison\n    (reference comparison : H₂)\n    (M : StateModularDatum E)\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ)\n    (A : ObservableAlgebra E) :\n    (constructiveRelationalDatum (E := E) reference comparison M ω).firstVariation comparison A\n      =\n    ω (comparisonInducedDynamics\n      (constructiveRelationalDatum (E := E) reference comparison M ω) A) := by\n  rfl\n\n/-- The comparison-state phase form of the realized datum is the channel metric twisted by `K = Jε`. -/\n@[rep_depth krein, simp]\ntheorem constructiveRelationalDatum_comparisonGeneratorPhase_apply_eq_comp_complex_i\n    (reference comparison : H₂)\n    (M : StateModularDatum E)\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ)\n    (X Y : PerturbationChannel E) :\n    comparisonGeneratorPhase\n        (constructiveRelationalDatum (E := E) reference comparison M ω) X Y\n      =\n    ⟪(X.comp (InfoGeometry.Krein.complex_i (E := E))) comparison,\n      Y comparison⟫_ℝ := by\n  simp [comparisonGeneratorPhase, comparisonGeneratorMetric,\n    constructiveRelationalDatum, channelMetricAtState, channelPhaseAxis]\n\n@[rep_depth krein, simp]\ntheorem constructiveRelationalDatum_comparisonGeneratorPhase_apply\n    (reference comparison : H₂)\n    (M : StateModularDatum E)\n    (ω : EndH →L[ℝ] ℝ)\n    (X Y : PerturbationChannel E) :\n    comparisonGeneratorPhase\n        (constructiveRelationalDatum (E := E) reference comparison M ω) X Y\n      =\n    ⟪(X.comp (InfoGeometry.Canonical.TomitaTakesaki.modularComplexI (E := E))) comparison,\n      Y comparison⟫_ℝ := by\n  exact constructiveRelationalDatum_comparisonGeneratorPhase_apply_eq_comp_complex_i\n    (E := E) reference comparison M ω X Y\n\nend Core\n\nsection LightweightTheorems\n\nvariable {E : Type 0}\nvariable [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n\nlocal notation \"H₂\" => DoubledSpace E\nlocal notation \"EndH\" => H₂ →L[ℝ] H₂\n\n/-- The symmetric second-variation sector is invariant under swapping the channels. -/\n@[rep_depth transport]\ntheorem operatorInformationMetricPart_swap\n    (X Y A : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationMetricPart (E := E) X Y A\n      =\n    operatorInformationMetricPart (E := E) Y X A := by\n  unfold operatorInformationMetricPart\n  simp [add_comm]\n\n/-- The phase readout is the metric readout twisted by the concrete phase axis `K = Jε`. -/\n@[rep_depth transport, simp]\ntheorem operatorInformationPhaseReadout_eq_metric_comp_complex_i\n    [CompleteSpace E]\n    (X A : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationPhaseReadout (E := E) X A\n      =\n    (operatorInformationMetricReadout (E := E) X A).compLeft\n      (InfoGeometry.Krein.complex_i (E := E)).toLinearMap := by\n  ext u v\n  simp [operatorInformationPhaseReadout, operatorInformationMetricReadout]\n\n@[rep_depth transport, simp]\ntheorem operatorInformationPhaseReadout_eq_metric_comp_modularComplexI\n    (X A : EndH) :\n    operatorInformationPhaseReadout (E := E) X A\n      =\n    (operatorInformationMetricReadout (E := E) X A).compLeft\n      (InfoGeometry.Canonical.TomitaTakesaki.modularComplexI (E := E)).toLinearMap := by\n  rfl\n\nend LightweightTheorems\n\nend InfoGeometry.Canonical.RelationalInformationDynamics\n","mtime":1777928003337}